Root cause (quoted): the coder runs under the systemd confinement
`dispatch-storagegenie@SG-067.service`, `ProtectHome=read-only` + `ProtectSystem=strict`, with
ReadWritePaths=/home/andrei/StorageGenie /home/andrei/.codex /home/andrei/.grok
/home/andrei/.local/share/opencode /home/andrei/storagegenie-contract /run/user/1000.
`/home/andrei/.docker` is therefore read-only; `findmnt -T /home/andrei` -> `ro`; a direct write test
`touch /home/andrei/.docker/buildx/activity/.wtest` -> "Read-only file system".
`BUILDX_CONFIG` (the buildx config-dir env var, cf. `docker buildx version` -> v0.35.0) was relocated to
the writable private /tmp so buildx's activity/cache bookkeeping lands inside the confinement's writable
area. No privilege was used or escalated; the docker socket is the already-granted rootless socket
(`/run/user/1000/docker.sock`, context `rootless`).

